  "function_words_note": "Closed-class surfaces with the chapter from which they are licensed. Grammatical status (productive or receptive) is controlled by the grammar map: licensing lo/la as articles does not make object clitics productive before G03. Old forms a', da', tra' (= ai, dai, tra i) join ne'/co' at level 2; the editions' accents perchè and benchè are licensed from Part 4, where real text is quoted letter for letter.",
  "intro_en": "A course for readers of Latin who want to read Dante and the Florentine chroniclers. Lapo di Cione, sixteen, joins the Cerchi company's shop in Florence in 1299 and lives through the split of the Whites and Blacks to the trials of 1302. Fourteen chapters of graded story, rising from plain prose to the prose of Dino Compagni, then four units of annotated original texts: the chroniclers, Dante's political cantos, Machiavelli and Galileo's lectures on the Inferno."
